<title>USA: ANTEC, TSX shareholders approve merger.</title>
<headline>ANTEC, TSX shareholders approve merger.</headline>
<dateline>ROLLING MEADOWS, Ill. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANTEC Corp and TSX Corp said Thursday their respective shareholders approved a merger that will leave ANTEC as the surviving entity in a deal valued at $195.5 million.</p>
<p>TSX, an El Paso, Texas-based maker of cable television fiber optic cable and RF distribution electronics products, will complement ANTEC's line of hybrid fiber/coax products for the cable and telecommunications industry, the company said.</p>
<p>ANTEC is an international communications technology company.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
